{
  "slug": "agent-protocols",
  "name": "Agent Protocols",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Structured engineering protocols that make AI coding agents work like senior engineers.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **25 skills**, **8 agents**, **7 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (25): `api-and-interface-design` (Guides stable API and interface design), `browser-testing-with-devtools` (Tests in real browsers), `ci-cd-and-automation` (Automates CI/CD pipeline setup), `code-review-and-quality` (Conducts multi-axis code review), `code-simplification` (Simplifies code for clarity), `context-engineering` (Optimizes agent context setup), `debugging-and-error-recovery` (Guides systematic root-cause debugging), `deprecation-and-migration` (Manages deprecation and migration), and 17 more\n- **Agents** (8): `accessibility-specialist` (Accessibility engineer focused on WCAG-oriented review, keyboard and screen reader flows, and inclusive UI), `code-reviewer` (Senior code reviewer that evaluates changes across five dimensions -- correctness, readability, architecture, security, and performance), `documentation-specialist` (Technical writer focused on ADRs, API docs, and reader-first explanations), `performance-engineer` (Performance engineer focused on measurement-first analysis, profiling, and regressions), `release-engineer` (Release and platform engineer focused on CI/CD pipelines, deployment safety, and launch readiness), `security-auditor` (Security engineer focused on vulnerability detection, threat modeling, and secure coding practices), `spec-analyst` (Product-minded analyst focused on PRD quality, scope boundaries, and testable acceptance criteria), `test-engineer` (QA engineer specialized in test strategy, test writing, and coverage analysis)\n- **Commands** (7): `build` (Implement the next task incrementally — build, test, verify, commit), `code-simplify` (Simplify code for clarity and maintainability — reduce complexity without changing behavior), `plan` (Break work into small verifiable tasks with acceptance criteria and dependency ordering), `review` (Conduct a five-axis code review — correctness, readability, architecture, security, performance), `ship` (Run the pre-launch checklist and prepare for production deployment), `spec` (Start spec-driven development — write a structured specification before writing code), `test` (Run TDD workflow — write failing tests, implement, verify)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install agent-protocols@claude-community` from `arneesh/agent-protocols`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
